.TH LIGHTXR-GREETER 1 "2026-10-20" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lightxr\-greeter \- local and OpenXR display\-manager greeter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
/usr/local/libexec/lightxr/lightxr\-greeter [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the Qt login interface. In production the display manager supplies the authentication channel. The broker and presenter provide a curved XR panel about two metres ahead, controller pointing and an on\-screen keyboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-demo"
Preview without a LightDM/PAM connection. Authentication is disabled.
.TP
.B "\-\-windowed"
Use a window rather than the default fullscreen local view.
.TP
.B "\-\-bridge PATH"
Select the seat broker socket; default /run/lightxr\-broker/bridge.sock.
.TP
.B "\-\-help"
Show options.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&./build/lightxr\-greeter \-\-demo \-\-windowed
.SH SEE ALSO
lightxr(8)
